cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference ASTRA in your research or project, please cite it as below."
title: "ASTRA: Trustworthy Astronaut Health Monitoring & Mars Mission Simulation Platform"
authors:
  - family-names: "Hammoud"
    given-names: "Sondos"
    role: "Biomedical Instrumentation & Reliability Lead"
  - family-names: "Team Gravity Brains"
    given-names: "ASTRA Pioneers"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Mouhamad-MouSou-23278/ASTRA-MouSou"
url: "https://github.com/Mouhamad-MouSou-23278/ASTRA-MouSou"
abstract: >-
  ASTRA is an open-source autonomous astronaut health monitoring and Mars mission
  simulation platform developed for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026. Featuring
  a deterministic Trusted Data Layer (TDL) to suppress physical sensor artifacts,
  an 18-feature Random Forest clinical triage model, and an authentic 3D Jezero Crater
  surface simulation built on NASA HiRISE stereo topography, ASTRA addresses the
  22-minute Earth-Mars communication latency by providing earth-independent medical
  decision support conforming to NASA-STD-3001.
keywords:
  - "NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026"
  - "Astronaut Health Monitoring"
  - "Mars Mission Simulation"
  - "Trusted Data Layer"
  - "Space Medicine"
  - "NASA-STD-3001"
  - "FastAPI"
  - "Three.js"
version: "2.5.0-Audited"
date-released: "2026-11-15"
